    🔀 CHANNEL_UNIFICATION_VERIFIED — confirmed mapping (run mapping in BQ, not LLM):
    
    The NPI Channel column has TWO naming conventions in the same column.
    SAME CAMPAIGNS appear under TWO DIFFERENT names depending on data source:
    
    | Platform side (Cost > 0) | GA4 side (Conv > 0) | UNIFIED CHANNEL |
    |--------------------------|---------------------|-----------------|
    | Search                   | Paid Search         | Paid Search     |
    | Demand Gen               | Cross-network*      | Demand Gen      |
    | Performance Max          | Cross-network*      | P-Max           |
    | Paid Social              | Paid Social         | Paid Social     |
    | OTT                      | (no GA4 match)      | OTT             |
    | CTV                      | (no GA4 match)      | CTV             |
    | Online Video / Video     | Paid Video          | Video           |
    | Display                  | Display             | Display         |
    | Linear TV                | (no GA4 match)      | Linear TV       |
    | OOH / Print              | (no GA4 match)      | OOH/Print       |
    
    *Cross-network combines Demand Gen + Performance Max attribution
    
    USE THIS UNIFIED CTE FOR BLENDED CPA:
    
```sql
    WITH unified AS (
      SELECT 
        Date,
        CASE 
          WHEN Channel IN ('Search', 'Paid Search') THEN 'Paid Search'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Demand Gen') THEN 'Demand Gen'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Performance Max') THEN 'Performance Max'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Cross-network') THEN 'Demand Gen + P-Max (combined)'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Paid Social') THEN 'Paid Social'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Online Video', 'Paid Video', 'Video') THEN 'Video'
          WHEN Channel IN ('OTT') THEN 'OTT'
          WHEN Channel IN ('CTV') THEN 'CTV'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Linear TV') THEN 'Linear TV'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Display') THEN 'Display'
          WHEN Channel IN ('Direct', 'Organic Search', 'Organic Social', 
                           'Organic Video', 'Email', 'Referral', 
                           'Unassigned', 'Paid Other') THEN Channel
          ELSE Channel
        END AS unified_channel,
        Cost,
        Conversions
      FROM `<project>.Astrobot_<client>.vw_astrobot_<client_lower>_nc360_dashboard`
      WHERE Date BETWEEN @start AND @end
        AND Client = '<client>'
    )
    SELECT 
      unified_channel AS Channel,
      ROUND(SUM(Cost), 2) AS Total_Cost,
      SUM(Conversions) AS Total_Conversions,
      ROUND(SAFE_DIVIDE(SUM(Cost), NULLIF(SUM(Conversions), 0)), 2) AS Blended_CPA
    FROM unified
    GROUP BY unified_channel
    HAVING Total_Cost > 0 OR Total_Conversions > 0
    ORDER BY Total_Cost DESC
```
    
    KEY RULE: NEVER attempt blended CPA without this unified CTE.
    The query MUST run in BigQuery and return a small unified result set.
    
